        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Lennon, Yoko Ono\n- Products: \"Nobody Loves You (When You're Down and Out)\", Walls and Bridges\n- Companies: Apple Records\n- Concepts: Lost Weekend\n\nFacts:\n- John Lennon wrote the song \"Nobody Loves You (When You're Down and Out)\" and released it on his 1974 album Walls and Bridges.\n- Walls and Bridges was written, recorded, and released during John Lennon's 18-month separation from Yoko Ono.\n- Walls and Bridges captured John Lennon during the period he called his \"Lost Weekend\".\n- Apple Records issued Walls and Bridges on 26 September 1974 in the United States and on 4 October 1974 in the United Kingdom.",
